              },
              {
                "key": "cf-ipcountry",
                "value": "DE"
              },
              {
                "key": "user-agent",
                "value": "Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 17_0 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/605.1.15 Mobile/15E148"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"submission_uuid\": \"{{$guid}}\",\n  \"form_name\": \"book_a_demo\",\n\n  \"first_name\": \"Lukas\",\n  \"last_name\": \"Brandt\",\n  \"email\": \"lukas@berlin-fintech.de\",\n  \"phone\": \"030 12345678\",\n  \"company_name\": \"Berlin Fintech\",\n  \"job_title\": \"CISO\",\n  \"company_size\": \"1000+\",\n\n  \"consent_given\": true,\n  \"form_render_ms\": 41000\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/forms/demo_form/submit",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "forms",
                "demo_form",
                "submit"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Simulates what Cloudflare sends in production.\n\nThe phone here is a bare German national number with no country code. Without `cf-ipcountry`, the service leaves it exactly as typed — it refuses to guess a country, because guessing wrong CORRUPTS the number rather than merely leaving it unformatted.\n\nWith the header present, expect after the worker runs:\n  country_code = DE\n  device_type  = mobile   (parsed from the user agent; the client sent none)\n  phone_e164   = +493012345678"
          }
        }
